          "worked": "The intercepts are $(0,-2)$ and $(2,0)$. The line rises $2$ units for $2$ units to the right, so its rule is $y=x-2$.\n\nThe continuous line extends indefinitely in both directions, so both sets are $\\mathbb R$.\n\n$$\\mathcal R=\\{(x,y):x,y\\in\\mathbb R,\\ y=x-2\\}.$$",
